) -> Void)?"},{"type":"text","text":" alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" — a second button for something other than retrying, like going back to the previous screen instead of hammering a request that’s going to fail the same way again:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenStateDefaultErrorView(error: error, onRetry: reload, secondaryAction: (title: \"Go Back\", action: goBack))","ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView(error: error, onRetry: reload, secondaryAction: (title: \"Go Back\", action: goBack))"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" by default, so every existing call site keeps showing just Retry (or nothing, if "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" is also "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":") until you opt in."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"A user-facing message, distinct from localizedDescription","type":"heading","anchor":"A-user-facing-message-distinct-from-localizedDescription"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error.localizedDescription"},{"type":"text","text":" is often a debugging string, or — for a plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStringConvertible"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedError"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance — just the type name, not something to put in front of the person using the app. Conform your own error type to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError"},{"type":"text","text":" to supply a message meant to actually be read:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct APIError: ScreenStateDisplayableError {","    let displayMessage: String","}","","store.setError(AP